# Pet Clinic Rush – Architecture & Coding Rules
# Never break the build. TypeScript strict, no `any` without a comment.
# Data-driven content – no hardcoded magic numbers in logic.
# Pooled objects in update loops – never allocate per-frame.
# UI (Agent B) listens to events from gameplay (Agent A) only.
# Audio, haptics, saving always go through events/service interfaces.

# Project stack
# - Phaser 3.90, TypeScript strict, Vite 8, ESLint, Prettier, Vitest
# - Capacitor 8: core, android, haptics, preferences, app, status-bar, splash-screen
# - Portrait virtual resolution 720 x 1280, Phaser.Scale.FIT, autoCenter
# - Bundled OFL font: Baloo 2 (public/assets/fonts/Baloo2.ttf)
# - Data-driven content in src/config/, no hardcoded content in scenes

# Folder rules (src/*)
# - src/contracts/* – shared types, events, asset keys (read-only for gameplay; changed via contract process)
# - src/config/* – level/pet/need/customers/upgrades data (read-only for gameplay; Agent B writes)
# - src/scenes/BootScene.ts, PreloadScene.ts, GameScene.ts – Agent A owns
# - src/scenes/MenuScene.ts etc. – Agent B owns
# - src/objects/** – Agent A owns
# - src/systems/** – Agent A owns
# - src/treatments/** – Agent A owns
# - src/main.ts, src/config/gameConfig.ts – Agent A owns
# - src/utils/pool.ts – Agent A owns
# - src/utils/placeholders.ts – both (fallback generator)
# - src/services/** – Agent B owns (AudioManager, SaveService, HapticsService, AdService)
# - src/ui/** – Agent B owns

# Event rules
# - Gameplay EMITS: coins:changed, score:changed, hearts:changed, combo:changed,
#   timer:tick, level:started, level:completed, level:failed, pet:cured,
#   customer:angry, game:pause, game:resume, audio:play, haptic:pulse, tutorial:step
# - UI LISTENS to the above never draws HUD itself
# - Never import UI internals from gameplay

# Build & test
# - npm run typecheck must pass (no `any`, strict mode)
# - npm run lint must pass (ESLint clean)
# - npm run test must pass (Vitest)
# - npm run dev must boot to menu; full level playable

# Asset rules
# - Free only (CC0 / CC-BY). Documented in ASSETS.md and CREDITS.md.
# - If real asset missing, placeholder generator in src/utils/placeholders.ts keeps game playable.
# - Loader prefers real files, falls back to generated placeholders.

# Capacitor rules
# - android/ is Agent B's domain; gameplay never touches android/ directly.
# - cap:sync runs after build.

# Magic-number ban
# - All tunables must live in src/config/* or be passed as parameters.
# - If you find a number that feels like a tunable, put it in config and import it.